# Git Commit Conventions

Always write commit messages in [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format.

## Format

```
<type>(<optional-scope>): <short description>
```

- Description in English, imperative mood, lowercase after the colon
- Keep the subject line concise (aim ≤72 characters)
- Optional scope in parentheses when it clarifies the area (e.g. `note`, `2fa`)

## Types used in this project

| Type | When |
|------|------|
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `chore` | Maintenance, gitignore, tooling housekeeping |
| `build` | Build system, Vite, Laravel upgrade, deps that affect build |
| `refactor` | Code change without behavior change |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting, no logic change |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |

## Examples

```
fix(note): decrypt after save
feat: multisession
chore: remove build from index
build: upgrade to vite7
```

## Avoid

```
Stop tracking public/.htaccess and ignore error_log.
Updated stuff
WIP
```
